; sorts across `load` (doc/kurt-soundness.md §10.2, condition 10): a `default` doesn't cross `load`, the
; sorts it gave do -- a fact of a file with `default real` stays about the numbers in a file without
; a default (whose own unsorted binders are over all objects), one with `default any` about all
; objects; a constant declared `any` is over `any` in the loading file too
load natural
load helpers/sorts-across-load-real
load helpers/sorts-across-load-any

Pn 3                               ; a number
expect "TypeError" "must have sort `real`"
    Pn {1}                         ; a set: the place of `Pn` became `real` there (its default)
real k
∀ k (Pn k)                         ; over the numbers, as "all-pn"

Pa 3
Pa {1}
∀ y (Pa y)                         ; over all objects, as "all-pa"

expect "TypeError" "must have sort `real`"
    c + 0 = c                      ; `c` is over `any` here as there: no number
